WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.440
Even though many of the characters didn't
end up surviving the entire run of the show,

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.660
Game of Thrones' mix of established actors
and new faces has made its core cast into

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.950
household names across the entire world.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.980
In fact, you may not realize just how many
times you've seen them.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:20.119
As Tyrion Lannister, veteran American actor
Peter Dinklage has turned out years of impressive,

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:24.060
deeply emotional, and funny performances,
winning three Emmys for the role.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.680
Tyrion's biting wit, political wherewithal,
and surprisingly generous heart make him one

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.160
of the most complicated and fascinating characters
on television.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.120
Thanks to Dinklage's layered portrayal, he
has become one of the show's most beloved

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.120
characters.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.760
Dinklage was already well-known before he
was cast on Thrones, with his breakthrough

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.800
role coming in The Station Agent in 2003.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.989
His film career has only flourished since,
with appearances in comedies like Elf and

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:51.720
dramatic roles in everything from Three Billboards
Outside Ebbing, Missouri to Avengers: Infinity

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.720
War.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.940
The world almost missed out on Dinklage's
performance on Thrones because he promised

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.280
to himself to never take cliché "magical
dwarf" roles.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.700
However, creators David Benioff and D.B. Weiss,
with some help from author George R.R. Martin,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.620
eventually convinced Dinklage, the first and
only contender for the part, to sign on.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.560
"You feelin' strong, my friend?

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.780
Call me elf one more time!"

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.780
One of the primary contenders for the Iron
Throne, Daenerys Targaryen, has grown from

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.640
a meek young bride to a warrior queen with
a massive army and a litter of dragons.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.220
Daenerys has given the show some of its most
epic moments, thanks in large part to Emilia

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.870
Clarke's performance, as viewers might guess
from her multiple Emmy nominations.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.799
As a fearless leader who can do everything
from walking through fire to inspiring whole

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:42.310
civilizations, Daenerys has become another
of the show's most popular characters.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:47.340
Since she began her turn on Thrones in 2011,
the high-profile part has earned her plenty

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.340
of other opportunities.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.630
In 2015, Clarke played Sarah Connor in Terminator:
Genisys.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.340
She would eventually admit she was relieved
by the film's negative reviews and glad to

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.270
not be obligated to return for any sequels.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:04.310
Romance fans, meanwhile, might remember Clarke
from Me Before You, but her most popular non-Thrones

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.100
part yet came in Solo: A Star Wars Story,
where she played Qi'ra.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.460
Though Sean Bean only appeared in nine episodes
of Game of Thrones as Eddard "Ned" Stark,

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.800
his shadow has loomed over the series.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.050
The patriarch of the Stark family stands as
the Warden of the North before being dragged

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.180
into political intrigue in King's Landing.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.040
There, he briefly serves as Hand of the King
to Robert Baratheon, until ending up imprisoned

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.530
on charges of high treason for making it known
that Robert's apparent heir, Joffrey, was

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.470
not the king's legitimate son.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:37.450
Though Ned brands himself a traitor to stay
alive for his family, Joffrey beheads him

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.330
anyway, setting off a war.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.860
Bean himself has appeared in everything from
Troy to Goldeneye, but one of his most well-known

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:48.380
roles was in The Fellowship of the Ring, the
first film in Peter Jackson's Lord of the

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.380
Rings trilogy.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.780
As Boromir, heir to the throne of Gondor,
Bean played an honorable character who turns

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.720
treacherous then turns back.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.080
"One does not simply walk into Mordor."

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.200
He's corrupted by the power of the One Ring
before falling in battle protecting the rest

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.260
of the Fellowship.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.640
Thanks to the stand-out sacrifices of characters
like Ned and Boromir, Bean has become known

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.160
for dying quickly and spectacularly, making
death scenes something of a calling card.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:18.400
As Lord Petyr "Littlefinger" Baelish, Aidan
Gillen spent seven seasons playing the sneakiest

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.710
man in the Seven Kingdoms, whose constant
conniving and plotting help him rise quite

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.680
high before his eventual downfall.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.000
Though his supposed love for Catelyn Stark
is what seems to drive Littlefinger's actions

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.900
throughout the show, it becomes clear that
Littlefinger is out for himself, and when

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.530
he tries to turn the Stark sisters against
each other in the show's seventh season, he

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.840
meets his match.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.500
Long-time HBO fans likely recognize Gillen
from his similar role on another one of the

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.120
network's critically-beloved series, The Wire.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.560
He played Tommy Carcetti, a
politician who rises through the ranks of

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.180
the Baltimore government before ending up
as the governor of Maryland.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:56.340
Many film fans were introduced to Gillen in
Christopher Nolan's The Dark Knight Rises,

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.580
where he had a small role as a CIA agent.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.300
He has since said he prefers smaller films
to big-budget blockbusters.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.420
Cersei Lannister, multiple-time Queen of the
Seven Kingdoms, is one of the show's most

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.810
complicated and often despicable characters.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.410
A conniving strategist who is only out to
serve herself, Cersei's introduction to audiences

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.040
ends with the revelation that she has been
carrying on an affair with her twin brother

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.590
for years, resulting in three children.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:23.930
Distrustful of her younger brother Tyrion
and protective of her twin and lover, Jaime,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.560
Cersei has spent seven seasons waging war.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.280
After beginning her film career with a small
role in The Remains of the Day, actress Lena

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:36.900
Headey rose to prominence thanks to her starring
role in 300 and its sequel as Queen Gorgo,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.410
a powerful leader of Sparta who does everything
she can to help and protect her royal husband.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:46.370
Headey then took on the role of yet another
powerful woman, Sarah Connor, in Fox's Terminator:

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:50.800
The Sarah Connor Chronicles, for which she
received particularly positive reviews.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.480
During Thrones, she also appeared in a leading
role in The Purge.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:59.280
Throughout Thrones' run, Jaime Lannister has
gone from one of the show's most morally compromised

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.860
characters to one of its most beloved heroes.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:07.020
Known as the "Kingslayer" for assassinating
King Aerys Targaryen during Robert's Rebellion,

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:11.280
Jaime begins the show by trying to kill Bran
Stark, who catches Jaime in an intimate moment

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.280
with Cersei.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.480
After losing his sword hand in the third season,
he eventually turns his back on his sister

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:19.320
to help fight against the looming threat of
the White Walkers.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:23.960
His genuine friendships with lovable characters
like Bronn and Brienne of Tarth, as well as

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.990
his love for his younger brother Tyrion, have
humanized Jaime.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:31.670
Though he has appeared in plenty of Scandinavian
films, Danish actor Nikolaj Coster-Waldau

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:35.840
was likely best known to American audiences
pre-Thrones for his role in 2001's Black Hawk

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.840
Down.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.240
During his tenure as Jaime, Coster-Waldau
has appeared in everything from romantic comedies

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:46.280
like The Other Woman to horror films like
Mama and big-budget epics like Gods of Egypt.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:50.220
The Hound is yet another of Thrones' more
complicated characters.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:54.240
Even though he kills a child during the very
first season of Thrones, his nurturing side

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.560
also becomes apparent when he becomes intensely
protective of Sansa Stark during her doomed

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.960
engagement to King Joffrey.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:04.340
Eventually, he ends up traveling alongside
Sansa's sister Arya, who ultimately removes

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.700
him from her "kill list."

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.730
He later joins up with the magical Brotherhood
Without Banners.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.690
Fearful of fire after his savage brother,
The Mountain, burned him as a child, many

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.960
viewers are hoping he will exact revenge.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.220
"That's not how it ends for you, brother.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.580
You know who's coming for you."

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:24.639
Scottish actor Rory McCann has risen to worldwide
fame for the role, though viewers may have

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:26.740
seen him in a few films before Thrones.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:32.110
Aside from a supporting role in 2004's Alexander
alongside Colin Farrell and Angelina Jolie,

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:36.220
McCann's best-known movie role is likely as
Michael "Lurch" Armstrong in Edgar Wright's

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.220
Hot Fuzz.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:42.320
Played with cold perfection by Charles Dance,
Tywin Lannister will stop at nothing to keep

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.480
his family in power.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:48.020
He's a shrewd strategist and warrior, ultimately
helping defeat enemy forces attacking King's

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:50.030
Landing during the Battle of the Blackwater.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:54.310
As the Hand of the King for his grandson Joffrey,
Tywin enables Joffrey's cruelty and shows

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.780
nothing but cruelty to his own son, Tyrion.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.320
This makes him one of the show's obvious villains.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:02.030
Fittingly, he meets his end at Tyrion's hands.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:06.360
A role like this requires a veteran performer,
and Dance fit that profile perfectly.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.900
The distinguished British actor even earned
an OBE in 2006 thanks to his work on both

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.040
stage and screen.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.580
Since getting his start with the Royal Shakespeare
Company, Dance has appeared in everything

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:21.390
from the James Bond film For Your Eyes Only
to genre blockbusters like Alien 3 to prestige

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.080
television dramas like Bleak House.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.950
American audiences likely spotted him in his
supporting role in 2014 Oscar nominee The

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:31.740
Imitation Game alongside Benedict Cumberbatch
and Keira Knightley.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.600
As Margaery Tyrell, Natalie Dormer brought
a calculated, entertaining, and fascinating

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:40.550
presence to Game of Thrones, with many viewers
wondering if her manipulations would earn

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.060
her a seat on the Iron Throne.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:46.360
Originally married to King Robert's brother,
Renly Baratheon, Margaery ends up married

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.650
to Lannister kings Joffrey and Tommen.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:53.080
A generous spirit who genuinely cares for
Sansa, Margaery is a formidable contender

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:58.040
against Cersei, though she eventually meets
her end when Cersei blows up the Sept of Baelor.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:02.860
Before her turn on Thrones, one of Dormer's
best-known roles was as yet another calculating

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:06.540
queen: Anne Boleyn in the first two seasons
of Showtime's The Tudors.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.720
Dormer went on to appear in Captain America:
The First Avenger as Private Lorraine as well

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.360
as in Madonna's W.E. as the Duchess of York.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:17.520
During her run on Thrones, Dormer took on
another high-profile role as Cressida in both

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.940
installments of The Hunger Games: Mockingjay.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.990
Recently, she has earned critical acclaim
for projects like Amazon's Picnic at Hanging

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:27.380
Rock, a mini-series remake of a classic Australian
mystery.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:32.400
When it came time to cast Olenna Tyrell, the
"Queen of Thorns" and imposing matriarch of

00:08:32.419 --> 00:08:37.050
the House of Tyrell, a formidable actress
like Dame Diana Rigg could be the only choice.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:41.400
A wise and intimidating high-born lady with
an especially biting wit, Olenna would do

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.500
just about anything to protect her family.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.620
She even orchestrates the assassination of
King Joffrey.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:51.720
After losing her entire family in the Sept
of Baelor thanks to Cersei, Olenna sides with

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:55.400
Daenerys Targaryen, but is eventually cornered
by Jaime Lannister, who offers her a gentle

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.660
death by poison.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:01.000
Not content to go quietly, Olenna tells Jaime
just before her death that she is responsible

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.200
for Joffrey's death.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.500
"Tell Cersei.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.600
I want her to know it was me."

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:12.480
Rigg was very well-known before her multi-season
turn on Thrones, earning fame as Emma Peel

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:19.089
on the iconic '60s British TV series The Avengers
before becoming Tracy Bond, 007's only wife,

00:09:19.089 --> 00:09:22.640
alongside George Lazenby in On Her Majesty's
Secret Service.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:27.240
That paved the way for several projects to
come, including her eventual role on Thrones.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.980
Robb Stark serves as one of the show's moral
centers.

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:34.840
But by going back on a de facto engagement
to a daughter of Walder Frey, one of his family's

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.090
allies, he seemingly seals his fate.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:42.070
Ultimately, his marriage to foreign-born healer
Talisa costs him, Talisa, and his mother Catelyn

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:42.860
their lives.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:46.960
The scene remains powerfully upsetting, thanks
largely to the performances of Richard Madden

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.180
and his onscreen mother, Michelle Fairley.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:53.220
After his on-screen death, Madden racked up
a number of new opportunities.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:57.920
After parts in Medici: Masters of Florence
and Kenneth Branagh's adaptation of Cinderella

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:02.790
as the Prince, Madden made a departure from
period pieces and fantasy by playing a DJ

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.690
in Netflix's Ibiza opposite Gillian Jacobs.

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:10.240
Most recently, he gained international acclaim
for his leading role in the BBC series Bodyguard,

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.700
for which he won a Golden Globe.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:15.100
As Game of Thrones has progressed, so has
Jon Snow.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:19.240
After joining forces with the Wildlings beyond
the wall, he is stabbed by his own brothers

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:23.860
in the Night's Watch, but is eventually revived
to fight another day alongside Daenerys Targaryen.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:27.800
At the close of the show's sixth season, it's
officially confirmed that Jon is the royal

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:32.600
son of Rhaegar Targaryen and Lyanna Stark,
who married in secret before their deaths.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:36.840
Not only does this make Jon the top contender
for the Iron Throne, it also makes him Daenerys'

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:41.020
nephew, which is pretty awkward considering
that they consummated their newfound relationship

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.580
at the end of the seventh season.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:46.680
Actor Kit Harington lent his voice to the
well-received animated film How to Train Your

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:51.500
Dragon 2 and re-teamed with HBO for both the
limited series Gunpowder as well as the raucous

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.710
sports mockumentary 7 Days in Hell.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:58.640
In early 2019, Harington also made his Saturday
Night Live hosting debut, enlisting several

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.780
Thrones co-stars, including his real-life
wife, Rose Leslie for his monologue.

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.400
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:08.430
Plus, even more Looper videos about Game of
Thrones are coming soon.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:12.020
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

